{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And it was in the six hundred and first year, in the first, on the first of the month.</b> From here that a single day in a year is called a year. Another interpretation: <b>In the six hundredth year of Noah's life,</b> in the month of Iyar, in the second month, on the seventeenth of the month, all the fountains of the great deep burst forth etc., and the rain was upon the earth forty days and forty nights, which are from the thirteenth of Iyar to the twenty-seventh of Sivan, and on the twenty-eighth they ceased. According to this interpretation they call Nisan 'the first,' unlike the plain sense of Scripture, and so all the others. And all the months are solar months of thirty days."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The comment compares two calculations of the Flood chronology; 'unlike the plain sense of Scripture' refers to the first interpretation reading ראשון as Tishrei, while this second interpretation reads it as Nisan."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:29.791634125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}